{"id": "EUVD-2026-81697", "enisaUuid": "2b1068b9-1e72-31a4-ba6d-1ff6f31cf6a8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSv4.1: zero referring call lists before decoding\n\ndecode_cb_sequence_args() allocates csa_rclists with kmalloc_objs(), so\neach referring_call_list starts uninitialized. decode_rc_list() assigns\nrcl_refcalls only when rcl_nrefcalls is nonzero. A valid list with zero\nreferring calls therefore leaves the pointer uninitialized, and\nnfs4_callback_sequence() later passes stale slab contents to kfree().\n\nAllocate csa_rclists with kzalloc_objs() so every rcl_refcalls member is\nNULL from the beginning, including valid empty referring call lists.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:51", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ed54460caf5b5aa65ec03c9a6032d831f39f19f5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7510a5b9edec9d9536a4e69f10edfb2592e6cf7f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4d23937e1c41995c2f54af26c89b5e48a41c299", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f31f3c042e024aef437cda42f0424ae8d4594b6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8fa4804fe62ca4155a2d8fc2789d630376cbf2fc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90104", "GHSA-8hhg-gc4j-p2q8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.64, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b6cbc36-c0cf-31d6-adf2-35d0cde9a50a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4aed55cb-f13c-31cd-990e-b4a0dd7530b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4aece6a19cf7f474f15eb861ba74db4479884ce3 <f31f3c042e024aef437cda42f0424ae8d4594b6c"}, {"id": "4c3e9043-27ca-3d7c-a3a3-6499a2496841", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4aece6a19cf7f474f15eb861ba74db4479884ce3 <ed54460caf5b5aa65ec03c9a6032d831f39f19f5"}, {"id": "4dc0659b-351